<title>BANGLADESH: Bangladesh taka closes firmer in quiet trade.</title>
<headline>Bangladesh taka closes firmer in quiet trade.</headline>
<dateline>DHAKA 1996-09-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The taka closed firmer at 42.3700/42.3900 to the dollar in interbank trading compared with 42.3750/42.3950 previously, dealers said.</p>
<p>They said the taka remained strong in dull trade because of the weekend closure of most international markets.</p>
<p>Interbank call money rates closed steady at 4.25 percent to 4.5 percent.</p>
<p>-- Dhaka Newsroom 880-2-506363</p>
</text>
